  "url": "https://example.com/article",
  "inputHtml": "<!-- {\"url\": \"https://example.com/article\"} -->\n<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<head><title>Lazy image sources</title></head>\n<body><article>\n<p>Lazy images use explicit source attributes to replace placeholders. Metadata that merely resembles an image URL should not override those sources.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://example.com/blank.png\" data-src=\"https://images.example.com/data-src.jpg\" resource=\"https://example.com/wiki/File:metadata.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" alt=\"data-src\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://example.com/spacer.png\" data-original=\"https://images.example.com/original.jpg\" resource=\"https://example.com/wiki/File:metadata.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" alt=\"original\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://example.com/1x1.gif\" data-src=\"https://images.example.com/gif.jpg\" resource=\"https://example.com/wiki/File:metadata.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" alt=\"gif\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://example.com/blank.png\" data-lazy-src=\"https://images.example.com/lazy-src.jpg\" resource=\"https://example.com/wiki/File:metadata.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" alt=\"lazy-src\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" data-src=\"https://images.example.com/large-preview.jpg\" resource=\"https://example.com/wiki/File:metadata.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" alt=\"large-preview\"></p>\n<p>All photographs should retain their real source after extraction, including images with an external placeholder, a small GIF, or a large inline preview.</p>\n</article></body>\n</html>\n",
